# P13-007 Sample-Sharding Writer — Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:executing-plans (inline) to implement
> this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** `COPY (…) TO 'out' (FORMAT pfile, shard_samples {label: [iids], …})` writes a sample-sharded
cohort — one shared `.pvar`, per-shard `.pgen`/`.psam`, a `concat_dim:"samples"` catalog.

**Architecture:** Extend `src/pfile_writer.cpp`'s `FORMAT pfile` bundle. Bind parses + validates the
`shard_samples` map against the resolved IID list. The write path holds N per-shard sinks open over one
row stream, writes the shared `.pvar` once and each shard's genotype slice to its own `.pgen`, writes
each shard's `.psam` out-of-band from its IID slice, and emits the catalog last.

**Tech Stack:** C++17, DuckDB v2.0 CopyFunction API, pgenlib (`STPgenWriter`), the existing
pvar/pgen/psam sub-writers.

**Spec:** `docs/planning/P13-007-sample-shard-writer` (this branch). Read it — it holds the inversion,
the merge contract, the §4 decision (C), and the engineering.

