## Review Focus

- **Mid-stream failure across N shards.** An upstream error (bad cast) or a per-shard write failure must
  orphan NO staging across any of the N shards + shared `.pvar` + catalog. Test: force a failure after
  some shards opened; assert no staging files and no final files remain. (Task 2.)
- **Slice correctness across genotype shapes.** The per-shard slice must be right for a STRUCT genotypes
  column (subset of struct fields) AND a `samples`-identified LIST (index range of the per-variant
  vector). Test both shapes round-trip. (Task 2.)
- **Contiguity / exact-partition enforcement.** A group that is non-contiguous in input sample order, or
  that drops/duplicates/adds an IID, must be a clean BinderException — never a silent reorder (which
  would make the catalog's global ordinals misdescribe the output). Test each. (Task 1.)
- **Catalog partition ordinals.** `start/stop` are global sample ordinals, not per-shard counts; last
  `stop` == total samples. Test the exact ranges. (Task 3.)
- **Single-sample and single-shard edges.** A one-sample shard, and `shard_samples` with one group
  (== the plain bundle but via the sharded path), both write valid filesets. (Task 2/3.)

